<article class="env-lemma" id="08R1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08R1">Lemma <span data-tag="08R1">92.8.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map such that $\text{Tor}^ A_ i(B, B) = 0$ for $i > 0$ and such that $L_{B/B \otimes _ A B} = 0$. Then $L_{B/A} = 0$ in $D(B)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/08QQ" data-tag="08QQ">92.6.2</a> we see that $L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} (B \otimes _ A B) = L_{B \otimes _ A B/B}$. Now we use the distinguished triangle (<a href="/tag/08QS" data-tag="08QS">92.7.0.1</a>) 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  L_{B \otimes _ A B/B} \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{(B \otimes _ A B)} B \to L_{B/B} \to L_{B/B \otimes _ A B} \to L_{B \otimes _ A B/B} \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{(B \otimes _ A B)} B[1]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       associated to the ring maps $B \to B \otimes _ A B \to B$ and the vanishing of $L_{B/B}$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/08QH" data-tag="08QH">92.4.7</a>) and $L_{B/B \otimes _ A B}$ (assumed) to see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 = L_{B \otimes _ A B/B} \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{(B \otimes _ A B)} B = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} (B \otimes _ A B) \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{(B \otimes _ A B)} B = L_{B/A}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>